      "writtenOn": "2022-08-10T17:00:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This file is included by modules though, and they need to reference the __kmalloc_min_size and __kmalloc_shift_low variables because __kmalloc_index() is inlined into their code, so wouldn\u0027t we have to export them? I believe it\u0027s the same case for the kmalloc_caches 2D array, and that\u0027s why it is exported even though drivers shouldn\u0027t modify it.\n\nOne thing we can do to mitigate writes to these variables is by adding the __ro_after_init annotation. That\u0027ll prevent them from getting written to after the kernel\u0027s init phase has completed. What do you think?",
